# PG Expense Tracker — Final Implementation Plan (v4)

## Overview

A full-stack, production-ready PG expense management web application. Built with **React 18** + Vite + Tailwind CSS on the frontend and Express.js + Supabase PostgreSQL on the backend.

**Build philosophy**: Ship a working product first. Features like real-time, export, and analytics come after core CRUD is solid.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Supabase Credentials Required**: You will need `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` from your Supabase project settings. These go **only** in `backend/.env` — never in the frontend. The frontend talks exclusively to your Express backend, not to Supabase directly. See Section 8 (Environment Variables) for the full security model.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Balances are NOT stored** — computed on-the-fly from `expenses` + `expense_participants` + `settlements`. Always accurate, no sync needed.

> [!NOTE]
> **No Auth in Phase 1** — `created_by` / `updated_by` audit fields will be nullable UUIDs, usable once auth is added later.

