## 8. Environment Variables & Security Model

> [!CAUTION]
> `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` bypasses all Row Level Security. It must **never** appear in frontend code, browser DevTools, or any client-side bundle. It lives only in `backend/.env`.

### Security Architecture

```
Browser (React 18)
    │
    │  HTTP requests to Express
    ▼
Express Backend  ←── SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (server only, env var)
    │
    │  Supabase JS client (service role)
    ▼
Supabase PostgreSQL
```

The frontend **never** calls Supabase directly in Phase 1. All data flows through the Express API. `VITE_SUPABASE_*` vars are **not needed** in Phase 1 — they are reserved for when Supabase Realtime subscriptions are added client-side (Phase 13), using the safe **anon key** only.

### `backend/.env.example`
```env
