## 9. Standardised API Response Shape

All endpoints return a consistent envelope. No ad-hoc shapes.

### Success
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { ... },
  "meta": {
    "page": 1,
    "per_page": 20,
    "total": 143
  }
}
```
`meta` is included only on paginated list responses.

### Error
```json
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "EXPENSE_NOT_FOUND",
    "message": "Expense with id abc-123 does not exist.",
    "details": []
  }
}
```

### Error Code Registry

| Code | HTTP | When |
|---|---|---|
| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | 400 | Zod schema fails |
| `INVALID_SPLIT_AMOUNTS` | 400 | Exact split doesn't sum to total |
| `INVALID_SPLIT_PERCENTAGES` | 400 | Percentages don't sum to 100 |
| `NO_PARTICIPANTS` | 400 | Expense submitted with 0 participants |
| `SELF_SETTLEMENT` | 400 | from_member == to_member |
| `MEMBER_NOT_FOUND` | 404 | Member UUID doesn't exist |
| `EXPENSE_NOT_FOUND` | 404 | Expense UUID doesn't exist or soft-deleted |
| `CATEGORY_NOT_FOUND` | 404 | Category UUID doesn't exist |
| `SETTLEMENT_NOT_FOUND` | 404 | Settlement UUID doesn't exist |
| `MEMBER_DELETED` | 409 | Operating on a soft-deleted member |
| `DUPLICATE_PARTICIPANT` | 409 | Same member listed twice in participants |
| `DB_INSERT_FAILED` | 500 | Supabase write error |
| `DB_QUERY_FAILED` | 500 | Supabase read error |
| `INTERNAL_ERROR` | 500 | Unexpected server error |

```js
// utils/AppError.js
class AppError extends Error {
  constructor(code, statusCode, message, details = []) {
    super(message);
    this.code = code;           // e.g. 'EXPENSE_NOT_FOUND'
    this.statusCode = statusCode;
    this.details = details;     // Zod field errors, etc.
  }
}

// utils/apiResponse.js
const success = (res, data, meta, statusCode = 200) =>
  res.status(statusCode).json({ success: true, data, ...(meta && { meta }) });

const error = (res, err) =>
  res.status(err.statusCode || 500).json({
    success: false,
    error: { code: err.code || 'INTERNAL_ERROR', message: err.message, details: err.details || [] }
  });
```

