## What's Deliberately Excluded (Now)

| Excluded | Reason |
|---|---|
| `expense_receipts` table | Removed |
| Separate `payments` table | Settlement `status = 'completed'` handles Phase 1 |
| Supabase RPC / stored procedures | Service-layer sequencing is simpler and more maintainable |
| Auth / login | Future feature |
| `POST /categories` endpoint | Categories are seed data, not user-managed |
| Service Role Key on frontend | Security — server-side only |
| Soft delete on `expense_participants` | Hard delete + cascade |
| Soft delete on `categories` | Reference data |
| Stored balance columns | Computed always = always correct |
| Cross-table transactions | Supabase does not support multi-statement transactions in the JS client; complex operations must be split or handled via specialized logic |

