## 15. Deployment

| Layer | Platform | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Database** | [Supabase](https://supabase.com) | Free tier — 500 MB, 2 projects |
| **Backend** | [Render](https://render.com) or [Railway](https://railway.app) | Free tier available; auto-deploy from GitHub |
| **Frontend** | [Vercel](https://vercel.com) | Free tier; auto-deploy on push to `main` |

### Environment Setup Per Platform

#### Supabase
1. Create project → copy `Project URL` and `service_role` key from **Settings → API**
2. Open **SQL Editor** → paste and run `database/schema.sql`
3. Verify seed data in **Table Editor → members** and **categories**

#### Render / Railway (Backend)
1. Connect GitHub repo, select `backend/` as root directory
2. Build command: `npm install`
3. Start command: `node server.js`
4. Add environment variables: `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `FRONTEND_URL`, `NODE_ENV=production`

#### Vercel (Frontend)
1. Connect GitHub repo, set **Root Directory** to `frontend/`
2. Framework preset: **Vite**
3. Add environment variable: `VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com/api/v1`
4. Deploy → Vercel assigns a `*.vercel.app` domain automatically

### CORS Configuration
The Express backend reads `FRONTEND_URL` from env and allows that origin:
```js
app.use(cors({ origin: process.env.FRONTEND_URL, credentials: true }));
```
Update `FRONTEND_URL` on Render/Railway to your Vercel production URL after first deploy.

